    "The draft states that Firefox release notes indicate the `navigator.mediaDevices` property is removed on insecure contexts, but the provided evidence explicitly qualifies this as a future change ('In the future, Firefox will also remove...') that was already the case in Nightly builds at the time, not a current universal rule.",
    "The draft presents the requirement as a universal rule without noting that the evidence for the `NotAllowedError` on insecure contexts is specific to the `getUserMedia()` method documentation, while the removal of the property is a browser-specific implementation detail that may vary by version or browser."
